# vms-1f7 (SHOW PROCESS matches oracle): SHOW PROCESS field layout on VAX V7.3.
# Volatile: the header date/time and the hex Process ID (e.g. 2020021A — its
# trailing nibble can be A-F, which a bare digit-mask would NOT catch, so it is
# masked as a whole hex token first). The rest (User/Node/priority) is digit-
# masked. This pins the field-label layout (User:/Process ID:/Node:/Process name:/
# Terminal:/User Identifier:/Base priority:/Default file spec:/Devices allocated:).
ARCH=vax
DESC="SHOW PROCESS field layout (date + hex PID + node/priority masked)"
NORMALIZE='s/\(Process ID: *\)[0-9A-F][0-9A-F]*/\1########/; s/[0-9]/#/g'
COMMANDS=(
  'SHOW PROCESS'
)
# MACHINE_MASK (rd vms-1f7): the two header values that legitimately vary by
# machine and moment -- masked so the gate compares the labelled STRUCTURE:
#   1. the node name -- VAX "VAX1" vs OVMX's own SCSNODE (INV-1: OVMX keeps its
#      real identity). Same mask diff_surface.sh's guardrail selftest proves:
#      a NON-EMPTY value is required, so a blank "Node:" still reds;
#   2. the MONTH of the header date. NORMALIZE masks the date's digits but not
#      its month letters, so a golden captured in AUG never matched a run in
#      any other month. The month is part of the capture-time date, the same
#      volatile field as its digits; three capital letters are still required.
# NOT masked: "Devices allocated:"'s device name. The oracle's carries the node
# prefix (VAX1$OPA0:), OVMX's does not (the vms-dv1 remainder) -- a real
# difference, so the gate keeps showing it.
MACHINE_MASK='s/(Node: +)[A-Z0-9#]+/\1<NODE>/; s/^( *#+)-[A-Z]{3}-(#+ )/\1-<MON>-\2/'
